  <title>Unit 1 Overview and Readiness</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00028</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Unit 1 Overview and Readiness</md:title>
    <md:uuid>d94304fa-b166-4a4f-94f1-3be550318ee6</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>In this unit, students will:</para>
<list>
  <item> Write and solve linear equations and inequalities given multiple representations of relations. </item>
  <item> Determine the slope of a line given multiple representations of linear equations. </item>
  <item> Represent linear equations in various forms (standard, slope-intercept, point slope). </item>
</list>
<para>To accomplish these unit-level learning goals, students will complete the following lessons and activities.</para>
<title>Student Readiness for Unit 1</title>
<para>To be ready for this unit, students will need to be able to:</para>
<list>
  <item> Solve linear equations using a general strategy. </item>
  <item> Classify equations. </item>
  <item> Identify points on a graph. </item>
</list>
<para>This Unit Overview Video will provide a big picture look at the content found in this unit as well as the prerequisite skills that students need for accessing the content in the unit. </para>
<media alt="Placeholder for Alt Text"><iframe width="660" height="371.4" src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/_ach1gc2EAo;&amp;rel=0"/></media><title>Section A: Writing and Modeling with Equations</title>
